# UX-SPEC §3.3 / §5.1 — the Worktrees page answers the pointer: a click selects a row, a
# double-click opens it, a right-click and the row's `⋯` open the same row menu, and every item
# runs the action its key runs.
#
# The page itself — H1, subtitle, toolbar, column heads, comfortable rows and the detail panel,
# which is open by default at the harness's 1440 px — is the `worktrees-page` shot's job. At that
# width the subtitle is short of room: the shot shows `4 across 2 repositories · 1 needs
# attention` whole and the review segment after it cut short, because the segment gives way first
# (§3.3). The segment is an inline button, one caption line tall, so it never makes the header
# taller than a caption line (a compact button is 26 px).
fixture: busy
await idle 30000
assert screen == Hub && hub_pane == List && focused == worktrees.row[0]
assert targets["worktrees.new"] exists && targets["worktrees.filter"] exists
assert targets["detail.open"] exists
assert targets["worktrees.reviews"].h < 20
shot worktrees-page

# A click selects: the cursor moves, and the row's hover actions are drawn for it.
click worktrees.row[2]
await focused == worktrees.row[2]
assert lists.worktrees.selected.label == hotfix && hub_pane == List
await targets["worktrees.row[2].menu"] exists
assert targets["worktrees.row[2].open"] exists

# The ⋯ menu lists the row's verbs: Open, Open keep awake, Sleep, Inspect, Copy path, Copy
# branch, Kill session, Delete. Delete (item 7) asks first; Cancel leaves the row alone.
click worktrees.row[2].menu
await targets["menu.item[7]"] exists
shot row-menu
click menu.item[7]
await dialog.name == Confirm 10000
click dialog.button[0]
await dialog absent 10000
assert screen == Hub && lists.worktrees.selected.label == hotfix

# A right-click selects the row under the pointer and opens the same menu there; Esc closes it.
click right worktrees.row[1]
await targets["menu.item[0]"] exists
assert lists.worktrees.selected.label == broken
shot context-menu
key escape
await targets["menu.item[0]"] absent

# The failed-hooks row's `View log` opens Jobs. It also expands that hooks job's log, but this
# fixture's hooks job ran under the seeding daemon, so the run's own daemon has no job to expand:
# the expansion is pinned by `screens::jobs` tests instead.
click worktrees.row[1].log
await overlay == Jobs 10000
key escape
await overlay absent 10000

# A click on the filter field opens the same filter mode `/` does; its box becomes the editor.
click worktrees.filter
await focused == filter.input
type ho
await lists.worktrees.rows[1] absent
assert lists.worktrees.rows[0].label == hotfix
shot filter-editing
key escape
key escape
await lists.worktrees.rows[3] exists

# A double-click opens the worktree, exactly like ⏎.
click left 2 worktrees.row[0]
await screen == Workspace 20000
shot workspace
key ctrl-s s
await screen == Hub
quit
